"lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Foie_gras_IMGP2349.jpg"}},"dish/kue-talam":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kue-talam","n":"Kue talam","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kue talam is an Southeast Asia or traditional steamed snack made of a rice flour, coconut milk and other ingredients in a mold pan called talam which means \"tray\". The cake mold used to create kuih talam are either larger rectangular aluminium tray or smaller singular cups made from ceramics, aluminium, melamine or plastic."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kue-talam"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kue_talam"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Rice flour","ingredient/rice-flour"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Tapioca","ingredient/tapioca"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/71/Kue_Talam_3.jpg/500px-Kue_Talam_3.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"S Kartika","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kue_Talam_3.jpg"}},"ingredient/sichuan-pepper":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sichuan-pepper","n":"Sichuan pepper","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Sichuan pepper is a spice made from the dried pericarp (outer shell of the fruit) of a plant of the genus Zanthoxylum in the family Rutaceae. It is commonly used in Sichuan cuisine of China and in the cuisines of the Himalayas. Despite its name, Sichuan pepper is not closely related to black pepper or chili pepper. Instead, Zanthoxylum plants are in the same family as citrus and rue."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sichuan-pepper"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sichuan_pepper"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Kung Pao chicken","dish/kung-pao-chicken"]]],["Sichuan cuisine","cuisine/sichuan-cuisine",[["Laziji","dish/laziji"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Peanut","ingredient/peanut"],["Shaoxing wine","ingredient/shaoxing-wine"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/de/Sichuan_pepper.jpg/500px-Sichuan_pepper.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Matt K","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sichuan_pepper.jpg"}},"dish/masala-dosa":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/masala-dosa","n":"Masala dosa","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Udupi cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Masala dosa is a dish of South India, consisting of a savoury dosa crepe stuffed with a spiced potato stir fry. It is a popular breakfast item in South India, though it can be served at all times of the day and found in many other parts of the country and overseas."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-masala-dosa"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masala_dosa"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Udupi cuisine","cuisine/udupi-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Udupi Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"udupi-recipes.com","note":"Blog dedicated to traditional Udupi and coastal Karnataka vegetarian dishes.","url":"https://udupi-recipes.com/about-me","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a4/Dosai_Chutney_Hotel_Saravana_Bhavan.jpg/500px-Dosai_Chutney_Hotel_Saravana_Bhavan.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Mike Linksvayer","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dosai_Chutney_Hotel_Saravana_Bhavan.jpg"}},"ingredient/sourdough-starter":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sourdough-starter","n":"Sourdough starter","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Sourdough is a leavening agent containing naturally occurring yeast and lactobacillus bacteria. The term is used to describe bread baked with sourdough, while the sourdough itself is referred to as a starter.  In addition to leavening the bread, the fermentation process produces lactic acid, which gives the bread its distinctive sour taste and improves its keeping qualities."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sourdough-starter"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sourdough_starter"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Armenian cuisine","cuisine/armenian-cuisine",[["Matnakash","dish/matnakash"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"]]}]},"ingredient/honey-bean":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/honey-bean","n":"Honey bean","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[],"src":null,"wiki":"Honey bean","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-honey-bean"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honey_bean"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Nigerian cuisine","cuisine/nigerian-cuisine",[["Moin moin","dish/moin-moin"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Black-eyed bean","ingredient/black-eyed-bean"],["Black-eyed pea","ingredient/black-eyed-pea"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Crayfish","ingredient/crayfish"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Palm oil","ingredient/palm-oil"]]}]},"ingredient/farro":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/farro","n":"Farro","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Farro ( ) is a grain of any of three species of hulled wheat, namely einkorn, emmer, or spelt, sold dried and cooked 